./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Notification-Troubleshooting.md:**Scenario 1**: If the message in the gray box includes "mimecast.com": It means that our emails are being blocked by the server. In this case, you should contact your IT person or team to address the issue.
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Notification-Troubleshooting.md:**Scenario 2**: If the message in the gray box mentions "blacklist at org/.com/.net," or resembles the screenshot provided, it indicates that your IT team has configured your email to use a third-party email reputation or blacklisting service. Here's what you need to know:
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Notification-Troubleshooting.md:- The problem arises because we send mail from a cloud-based service. This means that the sender's IP serves multiple vendors, including Expensify. If one of those vendors is marked as spam, it can block all messages from that IP, even if they're from different vendors (including us).
./docs/articles/expensify-classic/account-settings/Notification-Troubleshooting.md:- The better approach is for the server to flag spam via DKIM and SPF (rather than solely relying on the sender's IP address), as our messages are correctly signed and encrypted to prevent spoofing.
