I have reviewed `src/libs/actions/Report.ts`. The function `deleteReportComment` is responsible for deleting a comment. It constructs an optimistic data structure to update the UI before the API call completes. It also includes success and failure data to handle the API response.

Here's the relevant code snippet:

```typescript
function deleteReportComment(reportID: string, reportAction: ReportAction) {
    const originalReportID = ReportUtils.getOriginalReportID(reportID, reportAction);
    const reportActionID = reportAction.reportActionID;

    // We need to have the optimisticData construction available for both online and offline mode
    const optimisticData: OnyxUpdate[] = [
        {
            onyxMethod: Onyx.METHOD.MERGE,
            key: `${ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.REPORT_ACTIONS}${originalReportID}`,
            value: {
                [reportActionID]: {
                    pendingAction: CONST.RED_BRICK_ROAD_PENDING_ACTION.DELETE,
                    previousMessage: reportAction.message,
                    message: [
                        {
                            html: '',
                            text: '',
                            type: 'COMMENT',
                            translationKey: '',
                        },
                    ],
                },
            },
        },
    ];

    // If we are offline, skip the API call and return
    if (isNetworkOffline) {
        Onyx.unsafeUpdate(optimisticData);
        return;
    }

    const successData: OnyxUpdate[] = [
        {
            onyxMethod: Onyx.METHOD.MERGE,
            key: `${ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.REPORT_ACTIONS}${originalReportID}`,
            value: {
                [reportActionID]: {
                    pendingAction: null,
                },
            },
        },
    ];

    const failureData: OnyxUpdate[] = [
        {
            onyxMethod: Onyx.METHOD.MERGE,
            key: `${ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.REPORT_ACTIONS}${originalReportID}`,
            value: {
                [reportActionID]: {
                    pendingAction: null,
                    message: reportAction.message,
                    errors: ErrorUtils.getMicroSecondOnyxError('report.genericDeleteError'),
                },
            },
        },
    ];

    type DeleteCommentParams = {
        reportID: string;
        reportActionID: string;
    };

    const parameters: DeleteCommentParams = {reportID: originalReportID, reportActionID};

    API.write('DeleteComment', parameters, {optimisticData, successData, failureData});
}
```

The issue is that when a message is deleted offline, the `message` is cleared, but there is no mechanism to prevent other actions, such as creating a thread, from being performed on the deleted message. The `pendingAction` is set to `DELETE`, which could be used to identify that the message is in the process of being deleted.

Now, I'll examine `src/pages/home/report/ReportActionItemFragment.js` to see how it handles deleted messages. This will help me understand how to prevent the user from creating a thread on a deleted message.

